{
  "name": "clock_rewind_no_revival",
  "description": "UDP TTL 10s. At t=12 the first mapping is swept and its port is reused by fresh flows; the pool is refilled. Packets carrying older timestamps (t=5,t=6) are evaluated against the high-water clock (t=12), never reviving the expired mapping: the stale outbound cannot create a mapping (PORT_EXHAUSTED) and the stale return hits the reused port and fails the endpoint-dependent filter.",
